    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 15</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And on Dæna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.6-2"/> lage he ah fihtewita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.star"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.7-2"/> ⁊ fyrdwita, gryðbryce ⁊ hamsocne, butan he hwæne ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.star2"/> furður<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.8-2"/> gemæðrian wylle.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.9-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ on Dena lage hé ah fihtwite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ fyrdwita, griðbryce ⁊ hamsocne, butan he hwǽne furðor gemæðrian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And on Dena lage he ah fyhtwite ⁊ fyrdwite, griðbryce ⁊ hamsocne, buton he hwæne furðor gemeðrian wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>In Denalaga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.1-2"/> habet rex fyhtƿitan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.2"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.3"/> est forisfactum pugne) et fyrdƿite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.4"/> (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.5"/> est forisfacturam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.6"/> expeditionis), griþbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.7"/> (id est infractionem pacis) et hámsocnam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.8"/> (id est inuasionem mansionis), si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.9"/> non aliquem specialius honorauerit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>In<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.4-2"/> lege autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.5-2"/> Danorum habet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.6-3"/> rex has (consuetudines<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.7-3"/>): uiolationem monetę, quod Angli uocant feohƿíte, dimissionem belli, quod Angli<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.8-3"/> dicunt ferdƿite, fractionem pacis, quod dicunt griðbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.9-3"/>, inuasionem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.10"/> in domo uel in curia, quod dicunt hamsocne, nisi rex uelit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_15.lnote.oe.11"/> dare quod suum est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Et in lege Danorum habet pugne reatum, pacis fracturam et domi inuasionem, nisi quid remissionis impendere uoluerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="180" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ on Dena lage hé ah fihtwite ⁊ fyrdwita, griðbryce ⁊ hamsocne, butan he hwǽn<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_15.robnote.fn.7"/>e furðor gemæðrian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="260" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And on Dæna lage he ah fihtewita and fyrdwita, gryðbryce and hamsocne, butan he hwæne ðe furður gemæðrian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>Und im Dänen-Rechtsgebiet hat er [der König, vorbehalten] die Strafe(n <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) für blutiges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.1"/> Fechten (Münzfälschung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.2"/> <hi rend="italic">Inst</hi>.) und Strafe(n <hi rend="italic">G B</hi>?) für Landwehr[versäumniss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.3"/>], den Bruch [königlichen] Sonderschutzes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.4"/> und [gesetzwidrige] Heimsuchung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.5"/>, es sei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15.lnote.de.6"/> denn, er wolle jemanden (um so <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) weiter [durch Jurisdictionsgewährung auch über diese Verbrechen] ehren.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And in the Danelaw he [the king] has [reserved] the fine for fighting (false coining, Inst.) and the fine for [neglect of] military service, breach of [the king's] protection and [unlawful] attack on a house, unless he wishes to honour someone further [by granting jurisdiction over these crimes too].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="181" ed="#robertson"/>And in the Danelaw he has the receipt of fines for fighting<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15.robnote.n.2"/>, neglect of military service, breach of the peace and attacks upon people's houses, unless he desires specially to honour anyone [by granting him these dues].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And in the Danelaw he possesses the fine for fighting and that for neglecting military service, <hi rend="italic">griðbryce</hi> (breach of the peace) and <hi rend="italic">hamsocn</hi> unless he wishes to honour anyone further.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="261" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And in the Danelaw the king is entitled to the fines for fighting and shirking military service, breaching the peace and home invasion, unless he wishes to specially privilege someone.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">The other MSS' ‘fihtwite’ is better than G's ‘fihtewita’ (but compare II Em 3). Quadr.'s þ = wynn.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 319, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 260, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “| flyman: omitted AB | þæt: omitted B | ær: omitted B”); AP: corrected against Whitelock p. 464, October 2026 (was “And in the Danelaw he possesses the fine for fighting and that for neglecting military service, griðbryce (breach of the peace) and hamsocn unless he wishes to honour anyone further.”, now “And in the Danelaw he possesses the fine for fighting and that for neglecting military service, griðbryce (breach of the peace) and hamsocn unless he wishes to honour anyone further. (expanded letters in italics: griðbryce, hamsocn)”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ðe: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">flyman: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ær: omitted B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät verb. aus</hi> fift.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected late from fift.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dan. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> Denel. <hi rend="italic">KHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Dan. T; Denel. KHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so DmRHk;</hi> fightw. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> -te <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus DmRHk; fightw. K; -te T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fir. <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> fyrhtƿ. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fir. R; fyrhtƿ. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. f. e. g. <hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. f. e. g. lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Dm;</hi> -ctum <hi rend="italic">KTHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Dm; -ctum KTHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so K;</hi> grydb. <hi rend="italic">Dm;</hi> grdebrice <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus K; grydb. Dm; grdebrice Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cna <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cna Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si — leg. fuit <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si — leg. fuit lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Denalaga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Denalaga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fihtw. <hi rend="italic">übrige besser; s. jedoch II Em.</hi> 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fihtw. the others, better; but see II Em. 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fyhtwite ⁊ fyrdwite ⁊ gryðebrec <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fyhtwite ⁊ fyrdwite ⁊ gryðebrec Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt übr.; s. o.</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">Anm.</hi>*</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in the others; see above 12 note *</seg></note>
